{"title":"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621a50d522ad9e2e8b3678ee3c5c2e4e06476683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDA&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> are the upper and lower bases, respectively, and edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825000b887cf170e8a54ee5dcdafffbdfb959cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD&#39;$\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel). The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> moves at constant speed along the perimeter of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> in the direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba5021fe27d82e2a3e3c293e409b60edaee4d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDA$\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> moves at the same rate along the perimeter of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8701771ab21f00a17b02edf89b1ada183f2bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;CB$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> in the direction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bf5c921abfaa19716cc897200cc255ca714771b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;CBB&#39;$\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> begin their motion at the same instant from the starting positions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Determine and draw the locus of the midpoints of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we prove a small lemma:  If the particles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> move along straight lines at constant velocities, then the locus of the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is also a line.  This is rather trivial, since all lines in 3D space may take the parametric form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce30307709566e3579caa512dd8109a76effa266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(at+n, bt+m, ct+p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> being time, and the average of two such lines must also have a linear parametric form.  \n</p><p>The locus clearly starts at the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb2c7600634636b0a25b56d087d112d6fbae523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, or the center of face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066c122a1654c7dbeb8526c1321ae9a8ad45163b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;A&#39;$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.  As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> moves from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> moves from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> move along straight lines, so the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> traces out a line segment, starting at the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb2c7600634636b0a25b56d087d112d6fbae523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and ending at the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc856e7f29652b2c928f2c025ed9befbab1873e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, or the center of face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbf5387b23aec52981bc69a54d203b9a373b038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCC&#39;B&#39;$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />.  This concludes the first phase of motion.  A quick check reveals that the locus goes nowhere during the second and fourth phases of motion, and only moves backward on the third.  Thus the locus is just the segment connecting the centers of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066c122a1654c7dbeb8526c1321ae9a8ad45163b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB&#39;A&#39;$\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbf5387b23aec52981bc69a54d203b9a373b038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCC&#39;B&#39;$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>solution is actually wrong, it's not segment it's parallelogram- author mixed the movement of points (even if he clearly understands what he is doing- just a little mistake) Here is correct soluton:\n</p><p>Answer: the rhombus CUVW, where U is the center of ABCD, V is the center of ABB'A, and W is the center of BCC'B'.\n</p><p>Take rectangular coordinates with A as (0, 0, 0) and C' as (1, 1, 1). Let M be the midpoint of XY. Whilst X is on AB and Y on B'C', X is (x, 0, 0) and Y is (1, x, 1), so M is (x/2 + 1/2, x/2, 1/2) = x (1, 1/2, 1/2) + (1-x) (1/2, 0, 1/2) = x W + (1-x) V, so M traces out the line VW.\n</p><p>Whilst X is on BC and Y is on C'C, X is (1, x, 0) and Y is ( 1, 1, 1-x), so M is (1, x/2+1/2, 1/2 - x/2) = x (1, 1, 0) + (1-x) (1, 1/2, 1/2) = x C + (1-x) W, so M traces out the line WC.\n</p><p>Whilst X is on CD and Y is on CB, X is (1-x, 1, 0) and Y is (1, 1-x, 0), so M is (1-x/2, 1-x/2, 0) = x (1, 1, 0) + (1-x) (1/2, 1/2, 0) = x C + (1-x) U, so M traces out the line CU.\n</p><p>Whilst X is on DA and Y is on BB', X is (0, 1-x, 0) and Y is (1, 0, x), so M is (1/2, 1/2 - x/2, x/2) = x (1/2, 0, 1/2) + (1-x) (1/2, 1/2, 0) = x V + (1-x) U, so M traces out the line UV.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO\" title=\"1962 IMO\">1962 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164000\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 230/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6440/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.723      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.723      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7541:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164000 and revision id 192805. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}